  "tolerance_note": "Every numeric quantity carries its own tolerance; lengths are in metres in the IFC project coordinate system (no georeferencing). Coordinate tolerances are 1 mm (1e-3 m). The independent integration itself is good to about 1e-9 m.",
  "computation": {
    "alignment": "Copy of the road-alignment design; x(s) and y(s) are cos/sin(heading) integrated with composite 8-point Gauss-Legendre on intervals <= 10 m. heading(s) is closed form from the line/clothoid/arc parameters. Independent of IfcOpenShell geometry.",
    "placement": "IfcLinearPlacement with an IfcAxis2PlacementLinear whose Location is an IfcPointByDistanceExpression on the horizontal IfcCompositeCurve (FootPrint) of the alignment. OffsetLateral is positive to the left; the local X axis is the curve tangent and local Z is up. The 1 x 1 x 1 box solid is centred on the local origin, so the world box centre is the placement origin: (x(s)-o*sin h, y(s)+o*cos h, v).",
    "bbox": "For a unit cube yawed by h about Z, the axis-aligned horizontal extent is |cos h|+|sin h| in both X and Y.",
    "counts": "Counts of the entities written below."
  },
